we slapped an experimental head rig on  his head and said now be the star of  this movie the actors behind the navi  and avatars dealt with long days limited  vision and heavily wired motion capture  suits there's a lot of work a lot of  body work and a lot of behavioral  work that i had to do long before  filming started the cast were brought  into the studio for a long and tiresome  full-body casting experience in order to  make these life-sized models the actors  had to sit with restrictive plastic wrap  all over their face while layers of  plaster cast were applied all while  unable to see smell or breathe very well  and this was just the beginning of the  process  while the cast had to suffer through the  arduous ordeal it was a major help to  the creative team who needed the molds  to create highly detailed scans to send  along to the designers that were then  able to create the incredible  transformation from human to navi or  avatar  all while keeping each character  visually comparable to the actor playing  them the idea that i had clung to for a  long time was this idea of mounting a  camera directly to the actor's head  those full body casts came in handy when  it came time to make specially fitted  head rigs that the actors had to wear  throughout their entire performance so  we wound up with a tight-fitting carbon  fiber  helmet this headgear was heavy duty a  kind of cross between a skull cap and a  helmet that were made to fit like skin  on the actors heads so they could keep  all the mocap markers steady these caps  weren't easy to wear since they had all  sorts of gear attached like wires  cat-like ears and even motion capture  ready hair not to mention the carbon  fiber arm with a tiny but powerful  camera on the end of it that reached  around to the front of the actor's face  while the addition of the camera was  necessary to capture the nuances of the  performer's facial movements and  expressions it could make actually  performing challenging as a camera in  front of the face could obstruct views  and get in the performer's way  fortunately the actors managed to break  through and performed with no bounds the  result is pretty incredible 100  committed performances  the mocap suits used in avatar truly  became like second skins for the actor  though they weren't always the most  comfortable skins  there is nothing natural feeling about a  full-body form-fitting suit kitted up  with wires and heavy battery packs  you've got a bunch of markers on the  actor's body that are being picked up by  hundreds of cameras very little time was  spent in the makeup chair as all that  had to be applied to the face were dots  for the motion capture and the wardrobe  department was really just the motion  capture suit department with the  distraction of all these technical  looking suits cameras and wires  everywhere an actor turned the one thing  they could keep a clear focus on was  each other's eyes since those were never  covered having that connection amidst  all the technology was key and a  definite motivator to help the actors  through when filming felt tough on top  of the actress's photograph then we  would turn her into a navi on top of the  body casts the team decided to obtain as  much visual reference as they could of  each cast member in the development  process each of the actors were brought  in for a special photo shoot one that  involved a giant sphere filled with  large bright lights and multiple cameras  surrounding inside the sphere the actors  were troopers through the process to  help the designers gather as much detail  about their physicality and facial  details the photo shoots didn't end in  the sphere though an incredible amount  of photos were taken while the actors  performed various activities including  archery and wacky facial expressions as  zoe saldana and sam worthington found  themselves running through the jungles  of hawaii they definitely experienced  the elements maybe a bit too intensely  for their liking i was i was naked  [Laughter]  for three days in hawaii since james  cameron wanted the actors to experience  these filming experiments as their  characters he had them in the actual  clothing their characters would wear and  that didn't consist of much we did a  couple of scenes and we ran around in  loincloth the fact caught the actors by  surprise as it never really occurred to  them just how minimal their actual  costumes were not an easy experience but  we have a feeling saldana and  worthington were very close after  enjoying that together if you haven't  gathered by now the preparation to bring  avatar to the screen was long and  intense but it did include a trip to  hawaii to explore and film in kauai  amongst the mountains and through the  jungles an incredible experience but  this wasn't a vacation this was work  which meant everyone had to deal with  the very real rainforest elements just  as their characters would have had to  the performers were even set up with  costume details like their tails and  their characters accessories while  saldana got to ditch the motion capture  suit for this she did need to wear what  her character would have and if you've  seen avatar you know it's not very much  this became especially tough on the days  when the weather wasn't so great and the  performers were facing all the elements  keep going let's go  every actor had to go through a very  intense training regimen before they  could even begin filming sam worthington  went through extensive boxing and  military training even getting the  chance to work with a former marine who  just happened to be james cameron's  brother john david cameron  worthington had to be confident enough  in his training to be able to give a  full performance while restricted by the  motion capture suit and helmet and he  definitely delivered  zoe saldana pretty much became an expert  at performing highly demanding physical  activities while wearing her full body  performance suit long hair on the cap  included the actress had to learn how to  shoot a bow and arrow both the human way  and the navi way left-handed and with  their hands reversed  while this was supernatural for the navi  it was far from simple for the  performers and the fact that they were  wearing their full motion capture suits  and headgear only added a layer of  difficulty and discomfort the training  was rigorous  two olympic team trainers were there to  whip the cast into shape and from what  we see in the movie they didn't  disappoint i had to take everything i  learned in training and applied to my  first day las alonso aka soote trained  so much that he was able to ride a horse  with speed and jump off all while  looking graceful this was vital since he  really was riding a horse when filming  and while in his wire and battery pack  covered suit these feats weren't just  difficult but dangerous as well wearing  the headgear meant the performer's view  could be obstructed by the camera in  front which is the last thing a person  would want riding a horse  the high-tech suits also spent some time  climbing up a model built in the studio  to represent the beanstalk the  performers were attached to wires with  heavy sandbags at the ends enabling the  actors to speedily scale their way up  translating to the animalistic  otherworldly movement we see on screen  as for the scenes when the characters  are soaring through the air when you see  them flying these things they are  working hard are we surprised the day  after filming these rigorous scenes was  always a tough one and left the actors  physically exhausted not to mention  overwhelmed by their second skin suits  as for the large group scenes terry  notary was brought in to lead the actors  through movement workshops and training  a rigorous process that was key for the  success of the film  hours were spent becoming fluent in the  navi physicality so they could all suit  up and perform massive dances like this  just seeing all the tech the performers  had to wear is overwhelming avatar is a  feast for the eyes and truly a triumph  for filmmaking these actors were nothing  short of brilliant to endure all they  did bringing their characters to the  screen while it wasn't under ideal  circumstances it seems like the hawaii  research trip was pretty incredible
 

